<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Why Choose an Above Ground Safe Room?</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Above ground safe rooms offer distinct advantages, especially for those seeking immediate and accessible storm protection. Unlike underground shelters that require excavation and can be difficult to access for some individuals, above ground units are installed directly within your home or business. This makes them an excellent choice for elderly family members, individuals with mobility issues, or anyone who prefers not to navigate stairs during a storm.</p><p>These shelters provide a visible, secure refuge that can be reached quickly when every second counts. They integrate seamlessly into your existing space, often within a garage or an interior room, without altering your property's exterior. This convenience, combined with their superior protection, makes them a practical investment for life safety.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Our Above Ground Safe Room Features & Installation</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Texoma Storm Shelters provides robust above ground safe rooms constructed from heavy-duty modular steel. These units are engineered to withstand extreme tornado forces, earning an EF5 rating for maximum protection. Our shelters are designed for secure installation, typically anchored to the concrete slab of your garage or an interior room.</p><p>Key features of our safe rooms include:</p><ul><li><strong>Modular Steel Panels:</strong> High-strength steel construction for ultimate durability.</li><li><strong>Secure Anchoring:</strong> Professionally anchored to your concrete foundation for immovable stability.</li><li><strong>Customizable Sizes:</strong> Available in various dimensions to fit your specific needs and space.</li><li><strong>Easy Access Doors:</strong> Outward-swinging, reinforced doors that allow for easy entry and exit, even if debris is against the exterior.</li></ul><p>Our licensed and insured team handles every aspect of the installation process, ensuring your safe room meets all structural requirements and local codes. We prioritize efficient and precise installation to provide you with a reliable sanctuary.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Understanding Safe Room Standards: FEMA P-320 & ICC-500</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>When investing in a storm shelter, understanding the industry standards is paramount. Our above ground safe rooms are meticulously designed and constructed to meet or exceed the stringent guidelines outlined in FEMA P-320 and ICC-500. These standards are critical for ensuring a shelter can truly protect occupants from the extreme forces of a tornado.</p><p>FEMA P-320, 'Taking Shelter from the Storm: Building a Safe Room for Your Home or Small Business,' provides guidance on safe room design and construction. The ICC-500, 'Standard for the Design and Construction of Storm Shelters,' is a nationally recognized standard that specifies minimum requirements for storm shelters. By adhering to these benchmarks, we guarantee that your Texoma Storm Shelters safe room offers certified, life-saving protection.</p><p>Choosing a shelter that is independently verified to meet these standards is vital. It means the materials, design, and construction methods have been rigorously tested and proven effective against tornado-force winds and impacts.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Above Ground Safe Room Cost & What to Expect</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The cost of an above ground safe room in Sherman TX and the surrounding Texoma area typically ranges from $4,500 to $9,500. This price range includes the safe room unit itself and professional installation by our licensed and insured team. The final cost depends on factors such as the size of the safe room, any specific features you choose, and the complexity of the installation location.</p><p>We believe in transparent pricing and provide free written estimates for every project. This allows you to understand the full scope and cost before any work begins. We can also guide you through potential rebate programs or financing options that might be available for storm shelter installations in your area.</p><p>Investing in an above ground safe room is an investment in your family's safety and peace of mind. We are here to help you find the right solution that fits both your protection needs and your budget. Contact us today for a detailed estimate.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What is an above ground safe room?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">An above ground safe room is a reinforced structure installed inside an existing building, such as a home or business, to provide protection from tornadoes and severe weather. Unlike underground shelters, it sits on the existing concrete slab and is designed for quick, accessible entry, especially beneficial for those with mobility concerns.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How much do above ground safe rooms cost in Sherman TX?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">The cost for an above ground safe room in Sherman TX generally ranges from $4,500 to $9,500. This price includes the safe room unit and professional installation. The exact cost will depend on the size of the unit and any specific customization options you select. We offer free written estimates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Where can an above ground safe room be installed?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Above ground safe rooms are versatile and can be installed in various interior locations within your home or business. Common installation sites include garages, closets, utility rooms, or even a corner of a living space. They are securely anchored to your existing concrete foundation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Are your safe rooms FEMA compliant?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes, all our above ground safe rooms are designed and installed to meet or exceed the rigorous safety standards outlined in FEMA P-320 and ICC-500. These standards ensure that the shelters provide proven, life-saving protection against EF5 tornado forces and projectile impacts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How do I get an estimate for an above ground safe room?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Getting an estimate for an above ground safe room is easy. Simply call Texoma Storm Shelters at (903) 884-7210 or email us at info@texomastormshelters.com. We will arrange a convenient time to discuss your needs and provide you with a free, no-obligation written estimate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
